<o:LogicalDiagram Id="o6">
<a:ObjectID>9650CADB-54FA-4EA2-9AFA-5365035CB2A6</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Wellbore</a:Name>
<a:Code>DIRECTIONAL_SURVEY</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The Directional Survey Data Area defines the data that pertains to the measurement of inclination and azimuth against measured depth in a well that is used to calculate the wellbore trajectory and directional drilling performance parameters.
 
Examples of In-Scope: 1) Directional survey points; 2) derived composite directional survey; 3) post-drilling directional survey (e.g., resurvey taken to support sidetrack drilling).
Examples of Out-of-Scope: 1) Other survey types that do not specifically related to defining well path trajectory, e.g., (induction) electrical surveys, temperature surveys, velocity surveys, check shot surveys, etc.
</a:Comment>
<a:Stereotype>DataArea</a:Stereotype>
