<o:LogicalDiagram Id="o216">
<a:ObjectID>ECD8F1C6-800E-4B77-B9A7-2DE8478D2107</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Well Activity</a:Name>
<a:Code>WELL_ACTIVITY</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The Well Activity Data Area defines the operation and performance data that pertains to activities performed on a well.
 
Examples of In-Scope: 1) The activities involved in initially constructing a new well; 2) the activities involved in drilling a new wellbore; 3) the activities involved in deepening a wellbore; 4) the activities involved in completing, working over, recompleting, or abandoning any part of a well.
Examples of Out-of-Scope: 1) Information about the work units that are used to carry out well activities; 2) information about the composition of the well to include: the actual or proposed hole in the ground (well) and its physical makeup (wellbores).
</a:Comment>
<a:Stereotype>DataArea</a:Stereotype>
