<a:Comment>The Well Data Area defines the data that pertains to the overall or surface point features of a Well and the physical properties of its Wellbores.  A Well is an actual or proposed hole in the ground. A Wellbore is an actual or proposed path through some or all of a Well that starts at a specific bottom hole point and ends at the surface. Well includes all data from the bottom of each Wellbore up to the top of the Xmas tree on the Wellhead.
 
Examples of In-Scope: 1) Technical properties of the well as a whole; 2) whether the well serves as an injector or a producer; 3) geographical information about the surface penetration point; 4) association to the operator of the well; 5) associations to peripheral surface facilities; 6) association to the Field Development Plan that governs the well; 7) overall well lifecycle state (e.g., proposed, abandoned); 8) subsurface assemblies; 9) physical wellbore openings; 10) technical properties of the wellbore such as bottom hole depth.
Examples of Out-of-Scope: 1) The rig/work unit that was used to create or maintain the well; 2) the activities that created or maintained the well; 3) logical segments of the well that can involve more than one wellbore (e.g., well completion).
</a:Comment>
<a:Stereotype>DataArea</a:Stereotype>
