<o:LogicalDiagram Id="o614">
<a:ObjectID>41BC0B2D-C869-4C2B-B2E6-8B6309E5FB3A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>SSW Facility</a:Name>
<a:Code>DRILLING___WELL_SERVICE_RIG_WORK_UNIT</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The Drilling &amp; Well Service Rig/Work Unit Data Area defines the data that pertains to an apparatus that is used to construct, expand or service wells (oil, natural gas, water, etc.). Or, to sample subsurface mineral deposits, test rock, soil and groundwater physical properties, and install subsurface utilities, instrumentation, etc.  They can be mounted on trucks, tracks or trailers, or can be more permanent land or marine-based structures (known as offshore rigs). The term rig/work unit generally refers to the complex of equipment that is used to penetrate the surface of the earth&#39;s crust or perform work within a well.
 
Examples of In-Scope: 1) A traditional drilling apparatus; 2) An apparatus capable of carrying out hydraulic fracturing; 3) An apparatus that performs non-drilling subsurface activities.
Examples of Out-of-Scope: 1) Activities carried out beneath the surface; 2) Information about the composition of the well to include: the actual or proposed hole in the ground (well) and its physical makeup (wellbores).
</a:Comment>
<a:Stereotype>DataArea</a:Stereotype>
<a:DisplayPreferences>[DisplayPreferences]

