<o:Entity Id="o356">
<a:ObjectID>B6535FC5-8B90-4DB6-B731-5BEFFB7DFC42</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Rig Work Unit</a:Name>
<a:Code>RG_WRK_UNT</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A complex of equipment or apparatus that is used to construct, expand or service wells (oil, natural gas, water, etc.). Or, to sample subsurface mineral deposits, test rock, soil and groundwater physical properties, and install subsurface utilities, instrumentation, etc.

Rig-Work Units can be mounted on trucks, tracks or trailers, or can be more permanent land or marine-based structures (known as offshore rigs). The term Rig-Work Unit generally refers to the complex of equipment that is used to penetrate the surface of the earth&#39;s crust or perform work within a well.

A Rig-Work Unit is a kind of Facility.

Rig-Work Units can be classified by Rig-Work Unit Types.

Rig-Work Units can be supplied and/or operated by Vendors.

Rig-Work Units can be used to carry out Well Activities.

Rig-Work Units can establish Zero-Depth Points.</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Futura Medium;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red64\green64\blue64;}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.18362}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\cf1\kerning24\f0\fs16 A complex of equipment or apparatus that is used to construct, expand or service wells (oil, natural gas, water, etc.). Or, to sample subsurface mineral deposits, test rock, soil and groundwater physical properties, and install subsurface utilities, instrumentation, etc.\par
\par
Rig-Work Units can be mounted on trucks, tracks or trailers, or can be more permanent land or marine-based structures (known as offshore rigs). The term Rig-Work Unit generally refers to the complex of equipment that is used to penetrate the surface of the earth&#39;s crust or perform work within a well.\par
\par
A Rig-Work Unit is a kind of Facility.\par
\par
Rig-Work Units can be classified by Rig-Work Unit Types.\par
\par
Rig-Work Units can be supplied and/or operated by Vendors.\par
\par
Rig-Work Units can be used to carry out Well Activities.\par
\par
Rig-Work Units can establish Zero-Depth Points.\cf0\kerning0\f1\fs20\par
}
</a:Description>
