<a:Name>Reserve Resource Class</a:Name>
<a:Code>RSRV_RSRC_CLSS</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The categorization identified by the Shell Petroleum Resource Classification System (PRCS) recognizes three classes of Resource Volumes that reflect varying levels of project maturity:  Prospective Resources (Undiscovered), Contingent Resources and Reserves (Proved, Probable &amp; Possible).  There are also multiple sub-classes within each resource class.  An individual project (or well) may be associated with volumes in several resource classes and/or subclasses. For example, 1X, 2X, 3X.</a:Comment>
