<o:Entity Id="o1618">
<a:ObjectID>5B2193D3-555F-41B9-B37E-95B054D23DDB</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Prospect</a:Name>
<a:Code>PRSPCT</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>An Exploration Area in which hydrocarbons have been predicted to exist in economic quantity. A prospect is commonly an anomaly, such as a geologic structure or a seismic amplitude anomaly that is recommended by explorationists for drilling a well.

Prospects can be geologically contained by Exploration Areas.
Upon discovery of hydrocarbons with economic viability, Prospects can become Fields.
</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Futura Light;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red64\green64\blue64;}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.17763}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\cf1\kerning24\f0\fs18 An Exploration Area in which hydrocarbons have been predicted to exist in economic quantity. A prospect is commonly an anomaly, such as a geologic structure or a seismic amplitude anomaly that is recommended by explorationists for drilling a well.\par

\pard\cf0\kerning0\f1\fs20\par
}
</a:Description>
