<o:Entity Id="o1259">
<a:ObjectID>0B428F99-1DCC-4621-882D-0A60DCD9D4D8</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Project</a:Name>
<a:Code>PRJCT</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A Project consists of Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) Elements and Lower-Level Work Activities. A Project cannot be nested within another Project. Projects are grouped via Programs.

A Project may exist to build a facility or to group activities by the function, or group, responsible for executing the work over a period (as in the case of a Completions &amp; Well Intervention Functional Activity Plan for IAP)
</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.22000}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\ul\f0\fs20 Confidentiality: \ulnone\par
A project, in the context of business or project management, can be considered confidential data depending on the nature of the project and the sensitivity of the information it contains.\par
\par
Confidential data refers to information that is sensitive, proprietary, or confidential in nature and requires protection from unauthorized access, use, or disclosure. It includes data that, if disclosed, could harm the organization\rquote s competitive advantage, financial position, or business relationships.\par
\par
Certain projects may involve sensitive or confidential information, such as proprietary processes, trade secrets, strategic plans, financial data, or other confidential business information. In such cases, the project itself and the information associated with it would be considered confidential data.\par
\par
\ul Criticality:\ulnone\par
A project, in the context of business or project management, can be considered critical data depending on its importance and impact on the organization\rquote s operations, objectives, or strategic initiatives.\par
\par
A project can be considered critical data if it contains sensitive or confidential information that, if disclosed or compromised, could harm the organization\rquote s competitive advantage, financial position, or business relationships. This may include proprietary processes, trade secrets, strategic plans, or other confidential business information associated with the project.\par
\par
The criticality of a project as data depends on the specific details and information it contains. If the disclosure or unauthorized access to certain details within a project could have a significant negative impact on the organization, compromise privacy, or violate contractual obligations, those specific details should be treated as critical data.\par
\par
\par
}
</a:Description>
