<o:Entity Id="o1147">
<a:ObjectID>B6814AE9-0DB0-4467-8DE5-09FC5821B793</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Production Schedule</a:Name>
<a:Code>PRDCTN_SCHDL</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Sequence and timing of which material should be produced by the facility, including reception of feedstocks and products disposition ( e.g. scheduling the jetty (vessels), trucks, railcars and/or pipelines). Production scheduling aims to ensure the feasibility of asset operations as well as to maximise the integrated asset margin. Scheduling is typically performed in a very detailed hour-by-hour way for the next 2 weeks whilst being less detailed for the remaining outer weeks of the scheduling period (typically 90 day outlook).


</a:Comment>
