<o:Entity Id="o549">
<a:ObjectID>0C9C2933-3629-42BA-A731-B9B60AE9E135</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Production Allocation Wellbore Interval</a:Name>
<a:Code>PRDCTN_ALLCTN_WLLBR_INTRVL</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A Production Allocation Wellbore Interval is a kind of Facility that represents the intersection of a Wellbore and a Completion; that is, the portion of a given Wellbore that has its production (or injection) fluids isolated by a given Completion.

Physically, a Production Allocation Wellbore Interval contains one or more Wellbore Openings.  For Production Forecasting and/or Allocation purposes, one or more Wellbore Openings can be treated as a single unit known as a Production Allocation Perforation Interval.

In Production Allocation, a Production Allocation Wellbore Interval is assigned a percentage of volume in the case to where there is more than one Wellbore for a given Completion.

The lifecycle state of a Production Allocation Wellbore Interval is dependent on the state of its Wellbore and its Completion.
</a:Comment>
