<a:Name>Production Allocation Perforation Interval</a:Name>
<a:Code>PRDCTN_ALLCTN_PRFRTN_INTRVL</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A Production Allocation Perforation Interval is a kind of Facility that does not directly tie to a physical component of a Wellbore; rather, it is a concept that brings together multiple physical Wellbore Openings for treatment as a unit, generally for forecasting and production allocation. Also, commonly known as a Wellzone. 

Production Allocation Perforation Interval is the lowest level of the Subsurface Facility Hierarchy (given that Wellbore Openings are not considered Facilities), and it can be linked to a Reservoir or a specific subset of a Reservoir, e.g., a Reservoir Segment or Payzone.

In Forecasting, a Production Allocation Perforation Interval can sometimes be referred to as an Objective.

In Production Allocation, a Production Allocation Perforation Interval is assigned a percentage of volume in the case where there is more than one perforation for a given Production Allocation Wellbore Interval.

The lifecycle state of a Production Allocation Perforation Interval is dependent on the state of its Production Allocation Wellbore Interval, which in turn is dependent on the state of its Wellbore and its Completion. </a:Comment>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{77894B2F-5C8A-41A3-AAF2-C1D07AC2DAD1},BIM-core,926={8DB6F0D8-502C-4315-805C-4AC30C42CB29},CommerciallySensitiveInformation,37=No Commercially Sensitive Information
