<o:Entity Id="o944">
<a:ObjectID>5CE763C8-EFE4-40DF-988B-0CFCB2C8DC86</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Dynamic Model</a:Name>
<a:Code>DYNMC_MDL</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Features of a reservoir such as pressures, temperatures, and fluid and gas compositions can change due to the movement of fluids or gases through any of the formations pore spaces. Since these are dynamic in their nature over short timeframes, once production is initiated models that encompass these changing features are referred to as dynamic models.
</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Futura Medium;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red89\green89\blue89;}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.17763}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\cf1\kerning24\f0\fs16 Features of a reservoir such as pressures, temperatures, and fluid and gas compositions can change due to the movement of fluids or gases through any of the formations pore spaces. Since these are dynamic in their nature over short timeframes, once production is initiated models that encompass these changing features are referred to as dynamic models.\par

\pard\cf0\kerning0\f1\fs20\par
}
</a:Description>
