<o:Entity Id="o541">
<a:ObjectID>AA4330DE-5216-432C-B76E-01564329880E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Facility State Type</a:Name>
<a:Code>FCLTY_STT_TYP</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The definition of a kind of fact that a particular Facility is in a particular lifecycle state at a particular time. That is, it is a possible lifecycle state.

Values:
- Proposed
- Future
- Operational
- Abandoned
- Suspended
- Cancelled</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Calibri;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Futura Light;}{\f2\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red64\green64\blue64;}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.22000}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\ul\f0\fs22 CSI:\ulnone  \par
The description provided for Facility State Type, which defines the possible lifecycle states of a facility, does not appear to be commercially sensitive information. It outlines a list of common states that a facility can be in, such as Proposed, Future, Operational, Abandoned, Suspended, and Cancelled. These are general terms used to categorize the lifecycle stages of a facility and are not specific to any proprietary or confidential information..\par
\ul Confidentiality:\par
\ulnone The description provided for Facility State Type, which defines the possible lifecycle states of a facility, does not inherently suggest that it is confidential information. \par
\ul Criticality:\par
\ulnone Facility State data represents the current lifecycle state of a facility at a given time, which can be important for tracking and managing the facility\rquote s progress or compliance with regulations. While it may not be considered critical data on its own, the criticality of data can vary depending on the industry, company, and specific circumstances.\par
\ul Entity Category:\par
\ulnone Facility State Type data represents the possible lifecycle states of a facility, which can be important for tracking and managing the facility\rquote s progress, planning, and compliance. While it may not be considered critical data on its own, the criticality of data can vary depending on the industry, company, and specific circumstances. It is important to follow your organization\rquote s data classification and protection policies to determine the criticality of different types of information.\par

\pard\cf1\kerning24\f1\fs16\par
\cf0\kerning0\f2\fs20\par
}
</a:Description>
<a:Annotation>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Segoe UI;}}
\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs19 For example &quot;Proposed&quot;, &quot;Operational&quot;, etc.\par
}</a:Annotation>
