<o:Entity Id="o1832">
<a:ObjectID>C389AA38-C3BF-4F6E-A0FB-0E6E7CADCB63</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Supervisory Organisation</a:Name>
<a:Code>SPRVSRY_ORGNSTN</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Organisation Management provides a hierarchical representation of administrative structures and reporting relationships within businesses, operating unit or department. The relationships between positions and supervisory organisations are the driving force behind a number of HR processes (e.g., staff appraisal, notifications, time approvals, etc).

Supervisory Organization is the foundational building block of the Workday system. Supervisory Organization may represent departments, divisions, or other groupings of people to perform work (i.e. teams).  It is based on superior/subordinate relationships (hierarchy) and is the basis for the manager role (assigned or inherited). Supervisory Organization groups employees to represent who reports to whom, drives staffing actions and can be used as the basis for all other organizational roles (e.g. HR Advisor, etc.)

In Workday, a supervisory organization groups employees based on their reporting relationships. It forms the backbone of the organizational structure, showing who reports to whom, similar to an organizational chart. Each supervisory organization is managed by a single manager and includes all employees reporting to that manager.</a:Comment>
<a:Annotation>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Segoe UI;}}
\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs19 FWELL- PORG (April 21)\par
PORGD - in scope (Karen et al, May 2010)\par
OGEAP_CHANGE - renamed from DEPARTMENT to align with GF\par
PORG - as this is internal we can take GF definition\par
OGEAP_CHANGE - removed COST CENTRE attribute\par
\par
*** BUSINESS OWNER:\par
Human Resources\par
}</a:Annotation>
