<o:Entity Id="o1133">
<a:ObjectID>0C981D9D-4259-4BAC-9632-66D659B16A76</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Subsurface Realisation</a:Name>
<a:Code>SBSRFC_RLSTN</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>One possible interpretation (amongst many others) of the range of static and dynamic reservoir properties, geological structure and reservoir architecture based on all available (indirect and direct) data sources (well logs, core, analogues, seismic etc).  Given the general paucity of data available in the early phases of field development opportunity maturation, and that we cannot see the rocks themselves, there is considerable uncertainty surrounding what the subsurface properties are and how the reservoir might behave when under production.  Consequently multiple subsurface realisations are generated for each field development opportunity to capture and quantify the range of subsurface uncertainty.

Subsurface Realisations can satisfy Field Development Opportunities below the surface.

Subsurface Realisations can be evaluated in Field Development Scenarios.

Subsurface Realisations can call for Wells (in the Proposed State).
</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Futura Medium;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red64\green64\blue64;}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.17763}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\cf1\kerning24\f0\fs16 One possible interpretation (amongst many others) of the range of static and dynamic reservoir properties, geological structure and reservoir architecture based on all available (indirect and direct) data sources (well logs, core, analogues, seismic etc).  Given the general paucity of data available in the early phases of field development opportunity maturation, and that we cannot see the rocks themselves, there is considerable uncertainty surrounding what the subsurface properties are and how the reservoir might behave when under production.  Consequently multiple subsurface realisations are generated for each field development opportunity to capture and quantify the range of subsurface uncertainty.\par

\pard\cf0\kerning0\f1\fs20\par
}
</a:Description>
