<o:Entity Id="o1633">
<a:ObjectID>C1D7F561-ACD8-4E7F-8D38-9516C0A020E2</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Seismic Inversion</a:Name>
<a:Code>SSMC_INVERSION</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Seismic inversion is a type of inverse modeling used in geophysics, particularly in oil and gas exploration. 
It involves transforming seismic reflection data into a quantitative description of rock properties in the subsurface. 
This process helps geologists and geophysicists create detailed models of the Earth’s subsurface by converting seismic data into information about rock properties like porosity and impedance</a:Comment>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{77894B2F-5C8A-41A3-AAF2-C1D07AC2DAD1},BIM-core,939={8DB6F0D8-502C-4315-805C-4AC30C42CB29},CommerciallySensitiveInformation,37=No Commercially Sensitive Information
