<o:Entity Id="o938">
<a:ObjectID>ECF5D348-6E70-47E0-9161-53FFF0355C79</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Seismic</a:Name>
<a:Code>SSMC</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Pertaining to waves of elastic energy, such as that transmitted by P-waves and S-waves, in the frequency range of approximately 1 to 100 Hz. Seismic energy is studied by scientists to interpret the composition, fluid content, extent and geometry of rocks in the subsurface.
</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Futura Medium;}{\f1\fnil Segoe UI;}{\f2\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red89\green89\blue89;}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.17763}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\cf1\kerning24\f0\fs16 Pertaining to waves of elastic energy, such as that transmitted by P-waves and S-waves, in the frequency range of approximately 1 to 100 Hz. Seismic energy is studied by scientists to interpret the composition, fluid content, extent and geometry of rocks in the subsurface.\par
\par
Specifically, in this model, Seismic pertains to the\cf0\kerning0\f1\fs18  raw seismic data as obtained via a 2D or 3D seismic survey.\par
\cf1\kerning24\f0\fs16\par

\pard\cf0\kerning0\f2\fs20\par
}
</a:Description>
