<a:Code>GLGC_MRKR</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Any feature within the earth that is distinctive and easily recognized over a wide area, especially in the subsurface.  It identifies a feature related to the composition, deposition or relationship of the rock layers. Geologic Markers are primary identified on logs, but may also be identified in a cored interval, outcrop, or geochemical analysis.  Examples of markers include:  tops and bases of intervals, fossil occurrence, and uncomformities.</a:Comment>
