<o:Entity Id="o946">
<a:ObjectID>D7DF9A6C-E5DC-461D-9F60-5B52A75872A2</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Geologic Model</a:Name>
<a:Code>GLGC_MDL</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Geological models are created by geologists and geophysicists and aim to provide a static description of the reservoir, prior to production. The Geologic Model may include or be related to: well-to-seismic correlation, horizon / structure interpretation, velocity modelling, domain conversion, seismic attribute modelling and structural modelling (see definition below).
</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Futura Medium;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red89\green89\blue89;}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.17763}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\cf1\kerning24\f0\fs16 Geological models are created by geologists and geophysicists and aim to provide a static description of the reservoir, prior to production. The Geologic Model may include or be related to: well-to-seismic correlation, horizon / structure interpretation, velocity modelling, domain conversion, seismic attribute modelling and structural modelling (see definition below).\par

\pard\cf0\kerning0\f1\fs20\par
}
</a:Description>
