<o:Entity Id="o1441">
<a:ObjectID>EEAF9737-B6E7-40EE-843E-FB0ACDB9AF61</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>It Project</a:Name>
<a:Code>IT_PRJCT</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>IT-Projects carried out that are either:
- Stand-alone, either CAPEX or OPEX and run by DS, US or P&amp;T. For example: IT Projects part of data Move Programme or SAP implementation.
- Part of a Capital Project and hence CAPEX, run by  DS, US or P&amp;T. Delivery Verticals, and, for example Vendor Catalogue implementation.

These follow PDF Framework, but it is suspected this may not always be the case. These latter are then &quot;under the radar&quot; IT-Projects. IT Projects include RIDAC (Risk, Issue, Decisions, Actions, and Change). IT Product is currently managed as a project.
</a:Comment>
<a:Annotation>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Segoe UI;}}
\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs19 *** PURPOSE:\par
NO ATTRIBUTES AND/OR SPECIAL RELATIONSHIPS PLACED HERE.\par
\par
This is shown because it is a valid Project Type even though it belongs according to currect EDC definitions in IT-Project domain.\par
}</a:Annotation>
