<a:Name>Organisation_Type</a:Name>
<a:Code>ORGNSTN_TYP</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818155</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The first level of subtypes of Organizations.  Examples Include: Company, Department and Government Agency.</a:Comment>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2167">
<a:ObjectID>CB660751-BCFD-4C50-86FE-255BF862EA47</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Global_Location_Number</a:Name>
<a:Code>GLBL_LCTN_NMBR</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818155</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The Global Location Number (GLN) - former Internal Location Number (ILN) - assigned by GS1 organizations identifies physical locations or legal entities uniquely. It consists of 13 digits, the last digit being the check digit. There are two categories of location numbers: Participants who only need an GLN to clearly and unmistakably identify themselves for communication with the business partner are given a category 1 GLN. This cannot be used to identify articles by means of EAN. Participants who wish to assign the location numbers for their own enterprise areas are given a category 2 GLN. For a category 2 GLN, digits 1-7,
1-8 or 1-9 are described as basis number. This is used as basis for the creation of article numbers (EAN).</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>VA13</a:DataType>
<a:Length>13</a:Length>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2160">
<a:ObjectID>393E0E57-62DD-4ACA-8B92-D58428470FA8</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ISO_Country_Code</a:Name>
<a:Code>IS_CNTRY_CD</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818155</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The two-letter country code, defined by the International Organization for Standardization (ISO) ISO 3166-1 scheme identifying the country of the business entity .</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A2</a:DataType>
<a:Length>2</a:Length>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2155">
<a:ObjectID>58DCD6BA-4147-4E13-8378-3CCA235E0764</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Data_Provider_Organisation_ID</a:Name>
<a:Code>DT_PRVDR_ORGNSTN_ID</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818155</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A unique organisation ID allocated by the data provider (generally Dun &amp; Bradstreet) to the granular level of the organisation
==========================================================
Data Universal Numbering System (DUNS) 
A data universal numbering system or DUNS number is a unique, nine-digit series of numerals that identifies a business. Dun &amp; Bradstreet (D&amp;B) creates the number, which generates a business profile in its database and provides a company&#39;s name, phone number, address, number of workers and line of business, along with other relevant corporate information.

The legal organisation hierarchies e.g. Global Ultimate Parent, Domestic Ultimate Parent can be obtained via the DUNS Number.

A DUNS number is sometimes formatted with embedded dashes to promote readability, such as &quot;15-048-3782&quot;. Modern usage typically omits dashes, and shows the number as in the form &quot;150483782&quot;. The dashes are not part of D&amp;B&#39;s official definition of the DUNS number.

The DUNS_Number is a critical attribute for Shell&#39;s customer centric strategy because it is instrumental to provide the Single View of the Customer.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>I</a:DataType>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2168">
<a:ObjectID>FCBF41D7-C619-4990-A5FB-7123BCEFFCE0</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Data_Provider_Domestic_Ultimate_ID</a:Name>
<a:Code>DT_PRVDR_DMSTC_ULTMT_ID</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>top of the hierarchy within a country</a:Comment>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2169">
<a:ObjectID>283BF5EA-6EEB-44A9-9987-04AD4AB1FC11</a:ObjectID>
