<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A valuation class is a way of grouping materials with similar accounting properties in material management.Note there may be multiple valuation classes defined for instance per valuation area (the organizational level at which valuation is performed) and per valuation category/type.</a:Comment>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2207">
<a:ObjectID>9120B41C-10B3-4210-BA4E-FCC58624FFFC</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Material_Type_Tax_Classifications</a:Name>
<a:Code>MTRL_TYP_TX_CLASSIFICATIONS</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Tax classification provides the taxability of the material type for every purchasing transaction. It determines whether the material is tax-exempt, partially taxable, or fully taxable, depending on the customer and the jurisdiction.</a:Comment>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2208">
<a:ObjectID>C47F892E-243E-4368-ACCE-7318C0E0477C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Material_Type_Tax_Indicators</a:Name>
<a:Code>MTRL_TYP_TX_INDICATORS</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The tax classification indicator on the material type provides the taxability of the material type for every purchasing transaction. This indicator and the ship-to/ship-from jurisdictions provide the information necessary to calculate the sales or use tax.</a:Comment>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2209">
<a:ObjectID>223320FF-32CA-4CCD-8F07-AE5FD83D9531</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Material_Type_Industry_Sector</a:Name>
<a:Code>MTRL_TYP_INDSTRY_SCTR</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The basic materials sector is an industry category made up of businesses engaged in the discovery, development, and processing of raw materials. The sector includes companies engaged in mining and metal refining, chemical products, and forestry products.</a:Comment>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2210">
<a:ObjectID>42662F53-8362-4B20-941B-132AC6708EC3</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Material_Type_Descriptions</a:Name>
<a:Code>MTRL_TYP_DESCRIPTIONS</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The Material Type Description explains in words what the Material Type is about. Note that the description may be expressed in multiple languages, hence multiple descriptions may exist.</a:Comment>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
</o:EntityAttribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Entity>
<o:Entity Id="o543">
<a:ObjectID>A3D9C109-7DA9-4B73-A0BE-0DC7C7E8B4D0</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Material Stream</a:Name>
<a:Code>MTRL_STRM</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The fact that a particular MATERIAL TYPE can be measured as it passes into or out of a PORT.

There is one MATERIAL STREAM for each unique combination of Port + Material Type + Flow Direction.

A MATERIAL STREAM continues to exist, even if its OPERATIONAL STATUS is &quot;Off&quot;.</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.18362}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs20 The fact that a particular MATERIAL TYPE can be measured as it passes into or out of a PORT.\par
\par
There is one MATERIAL STREAM for each unique combination of Port + Material Type + Flow Direction.\par
\par
A MATERIAL STREAM continues to exist, even if its OPERATIONAL STATUS is &quot;Off&quot;.\par
}
</a:Description>
