<o:Entity Id="o600">
<a:ObjectID>97359AB7-7ECC-41CB-A44D-49F22B094D74</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Marker</a:Name>
<a:Code>MRKR</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Any feature within the earth that is distinctive and easily recognized over a wide area, especially in the subsurface.  Generically, a marker can be any surface of interest that can be &quot;easily&quot; identified and correlated.  Markers are primary identified on logs, but may also be identified in a cored interval, outcrop, or geochemical analysis.  Examples of markers include: tops and bases of intervals, fluid contacts (oil-water contacts, gas-oil contacts, etc.), fossil occurrence, and unconformities.</a:Comment>
