<o:Entity Id="o160">
<a:ObjectID>995BB3F5-6BEF-4051-86BF-169B2C06391A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Log</a:Name>
<a:Code>LG</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A Log (or Well Log) is a detailed record of geologic formations penetrated by a wellbore, based either on visual inspection of samples brought to the surface or on physical measurements made by instruments lowered into the hole. Well logs can be edited, processed, and/or interpreted by petrophysicists or other geoscientists to refine, combine, and/or enhance the logs. Well logs can be created during any phase of a well&#39;s history; drilling, completing, producing and abandoning. Well logs are created wellbores drilled for the oil and gas, groundwater, mineral and geothermal exploration, as well as part of environmental and geotechnical studies.</a:Comment>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{C6AC31EB-C90E-4811-BE11-ED1545ECDA32},SHL_CDM_EntityPropertyExtension,1049={0B6B8263-E277-43E7-A4EC-90E8C0E627AB},MTED_EDaM_Entity_Availability_Indication,13=&lt;unspecified&gt;
