<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A sequence of rock layers (AKA. intervals) that occur within an area of geological study. A stratigraphic column is a list of markers, which subdivides the column into intervals. The column is typically arranged such that the geologically oldest intervals are on the bottom and the geologically youngest intervals are on top.</a:Comment>
