<o:Entity Id="o1145">
<a:ObjectID>F9360018-8512-4A56-B410-7821820FE858</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Legal Hold</a:Name>
<a:Code>LGL_HLD</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Identification of information that is relevant for a legal matter and that needs to be located and safeguarded against disposal. Only applies for some litigation matters.


It arises from the legal preservation obligations or preservations of materials kept for potential use as evidence is required in certain jurisdictions when a Shell company is involved in litigation or other legal proceedings. Even when there is no formal legal preservation requirements, best practices dictate taking appropiate stepts to ensure evidence is preserved so that legal claims and defenses are not compromised (A shell company reasonably anticipates a legal proceeding being litigation or others).

Preservation obligations are tied directly to a specific legal matter (litigation case, arbitration, tax dispute, regulatory investigation, investigation by criminal authorities, etc.). The scope of the materials that need to be preserved is defined by the factual and legal issues involved in that matter – the scope should be defined by subject matter and by time.

The preservation obligation will terminate once the matter and any related legal proceedings are fully resolved – this may be a matter of months or it may take several years.</a:Comment>
