<o:Entity Id="o1426">
<a:ObjectID>6A1415D9-B9B9-452A-9581-C0855E9CFF28</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Language</a:Name>
<a:Code>LNGG</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Words, their pronunciation, and the methods of combining them used and understood by a community. Standardised
identification codes for Languages are defined by ISO 369_2.

In Workday, a language skill refers to an individual&#39;s ability to understand, speak, read, and write in a particular language. These skills are often assessed and recorded to help match employees with roles that require specific language proficiencies. Language skills are part of the broader competencies that Workday tracks to ensure employees have the necessary abilities to perform their job effectively.</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang2057{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.17763}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs20 Words, their pronunciation, and the methods of combining them used and understood by a community.\par
ISO codes for Language is 369_2\par
}
</a:Description>
