<o:Entity Id="o610">
<a:ObjectID>F920E046-3F47-4C8B-B8B7-38F10A853332</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Field</a:Name>
<a:Code>FLD</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>An area consisting of a single reservoir or multiple reservoirs all grouped on, or related to, the same individual geological feature and/or stratigraphic condition. There may be two or more reservoirs in a field that are separated vertically by intervening impermeable rock, laterally by local geological barriers, or both. The term may be defined differently by individual regulatory authorities. (SPE-PRMS 2007).  May achieve Field Lifecycle States over time.  These states may be: Under Development, Producing, Shut-In or Abandoned</a:Comment>
