<o:Entity Id="o1143">
<a:ObjectID>DA290890-2845-46F9-A245-6E891D1ADFC9</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Field Development Plan</a:Name>
<a:Code>FLD_DVLPMNT_PLN</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The Field Development Plan Data Area defines the data that describes potential and selected field development scope across subsurface, surface, and wells.  The Field Development Plan is often a legal requirement for governments and may be submitted to them for approval to ensure that due technical diligence has been applied by the operator.
 
Examples of In-Scope: Surface Development Opportunities and associated Risk Management Plans, Opportunity Assurance Plans, and Stakeholder Management Plans; Subsurface Realisations and associated Proposed Wells and Key Parameters; Field Development Scenarios and associated Schedule and Cost Estimates.

Examples of Out-of-Scope: Surface Facility Concepts and associated Proposed Surface Facilities and Key Parameters, Production Forecasts (although referenced), and Field Development Projects (for which Field Development Plans serve as the basis for design).
</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Futura Medium;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\colortbl ;\red64\green64\blue64;}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.17763}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\cf1\kerning24\f0\fs16 The Field development Plan (FDP) describes what the selected field development concept scope is across subsurface, surface and wells.  The FDP is often a legal requirement for governments and may be submitted to them for approval,  to ensure that due technical diligence has been applied by the operator.\par

\pard\cf0\kerning0\f1\fs20\par
}
</a:Description>
