<o:Entity Id="o1148">
<a:ObjectID>FD308442-8613-4D7F-A75D-5871208FA809</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Threat And Opportunity</a:Name>
<a:Code>THRT_AND_OPPRTNTY</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Threats and opportunities are occurrences which posses a hazard or brings benefit.  A threat is the occurrence which releases a hazard to cause a Top Event, for example, corrosion or operator error.  An opportunity is the occurrence which may bring benefit and produce a positive business outcome.  For example, change to equipment that produces more product for same cost, or a new line of business that RDS has synergies that allow for competitive advantage.  The scope of Threats and Opportunities within MTO includes, but is not limited to Process Safety, HSSE, Energy, Value Optimisation for Growth/Margins, Wells, Reservoir and Facility Management (WRFM), Integrated Production System Capacity (IPSC) Unscheduled Deferment / Unplanned Downtime, Availability and Cost impacting an Asset Total Capacity and Utilisation. Threats and Opportunities associated with Legal and HR and most confidential Commercial are not included.  However, only a long term Theat or Opportunity requiring more than 30 days for resolution is captured in the database and has MTO Score.  Short term Theat or Opportunity requiring less than 30 days for resolution is captured on visual board and not in any database and does not have MTO Score.</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.22000}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\ul\f0\fs20 Criticality:\ulnone\par
Threats and opportunities may be considered critical data for the following reasons:\par
\par
Strategic Planning: Threats and opportunities provide valuable insights for strategic planning and decision-making. They help organizations identify potential risks and challenges that could impact their objectives, as well as potential favorable circumstances that could be leveraged for growth or competitive advantage.\par
\par
Risk Management: Threats are essential for effective risk management. By identifying and assessing potential threats, organizations can develop strategies and mitigation plans to minimize their impact and likelihood of occurrence. Opportunities, on the other hand, help organizations identify areas for growth and innovation.\par
\par
Decision-Making: Threats and opportunities inform decision-making processes across various functions and levels within an organization. They help prioritize initiatives, allocate resources, and guide strategic investments.\par
\par
Competitive Advantage: Identifying and capitalizing on opportunities can provide organizations with a competitive advantage in the market. Understanding threats allows organizations to proactively address challenges and stay ahead of competitors.\par
\par
By treating threats and opportunities as critical data, organizations can prioritize their analysis and response efforts, allocate resources effectively, and make informed decisions to mitigate risks and leverage opportunities.\par
\par
It\rquote s important for organizations to identify and classify threats and opportunities based on their criticality and potential impact. This classification helps ensure that appropriate attention and resources are dedicated to addressing the most critical threats and opportunities, thereby minimizing risks and maximizing potential benefits for the organization.\par
\par
\par
}
</a:Description>
<a:Annotation>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Segoe UI;}}
\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs19 *** BUSINESS OWNER:\par
HSSE\par
}</a:Annotation>
