<o:Entity Id="o534">
<a:ObjectID>3634C480-392D-43EA-9A32-165D1D250A76</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Facility</a:Name>
<a:Code>FCLTY</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A capability to perform a business function or a service.  It is a token, or a concept used to describe the functional capability that may arise from the installation of Equipment and Materials.
Facilities do not have mass; they are not physical objects.  Only the Equipment or Materials that are installed to provide the service are physical objects.  The actual equipment or materials that are installed at a Facility can change over time and can be any type of equipment or materials that carry out the same business function.  Facilities enable business functions to be described independently of the equipment or materials that may be installed from time to time.</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Calibri;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.22000}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\ul\f0\fs22 CSI:\ulnone  \par
The description provided for a facility is a general explanation of what a facility is and how it relates to the equipment and materials installed to provide a service. This information is not specific to any particular company or industry and does not reveal any proprietary or confidential details. Therefore, facility data, as described in the provided information, is not considered commercially sensitive information.\par
\ul Confidentiality:\par
\ulnone The information provided about facilities is not inherently confidential.\par
\ul Criticality:\par
\ulnone Facility data, such as the functional capabilities and equipment installed, can be crucial for understanding and managing business functions and services. It helps in ensuring the smooth operation of processes and delivering products or services to customers.\par
\ul Entity Category:\par
\ulnone Facility data can be considered as master data. Master data represents the core and essential information about a business entity, such as customers, products, or in this case, facilities. It provides a consistent and reliable reference for various business processes and transactions. The description provided for facilities aligns with the characteristics of master data, as it defines the functional capability and relationship of equipment and materials installed to perform a business function or service.\par

\pard\f1\fs20\par
}
</a:Description>
