<o:Entity Id="o535">
<a:ObjectID>64C46DAD-777C-4964-9FB8-ED7D99B56013</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Wellbore Opening</a:Name>
<a:Code>WLLBR_OPNNG</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A continuous set of wellbore openings placed on the same day, where the openings all have the same characteristics (e.g., size, spacing), through which fluids may pass.  A WELLBORE OPENING  is defined by its top and bottom depth.
For example a WELLBORE OPENING may be a set of perforations in a casing from 1000 feet down to 1800 feet.</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.18362}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs20 A continuous set of wellbore openings placed on the same day, where the openings all have the same characteristics (e.g., size, spacing), through which fluids may pass.  An ACTUAL WELLBORE OPENING INTERVAL  is defined by its top and bottom depth.\par
For example an ACTUAL WELLBORE OPENING INTERVAL may be a set of perforations in a casing from 1000 feet down to 1800 feet.\par
}
</a:Description>
