<o:Entity Id="o658">
<a:ObjectID>7B8B6931-5617-4226-A9D4-D4D41B05DF2F</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Zero Depth Point</a:Name>
<a:Code>ZR_DPTH_PNT</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The default datum elevation used to reference other depths in a Well as aligned to a Vertical Coordinate Reference System.

Zero-Depth Points can define downhole depth origins for Wells.

Zero-Depth Points can be established by Rig-Work Units.</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.18362}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs20 The default datum elevation used to reference other depths in a Well as aligned to a Vertical Coordinate Reference System.\par
\par
Zero-Depth Points can define downhole depth origins for Wells.\par
\par
Zero-Depth Points can be established by Rig-Work Units.\par
}
</a:Description>
