<o:Entity Id="o542">
<a:ObjectID>3CF8CE54-E20B-4A2F-AA4F-9FECD63534D4</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Connection Port</a:Name>
<a:Code>CNNCTN_PRT</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A specific connection point where planned material flow occurs between the outside and inside of a facility.   Material normally  enters or leaves a facility only through a port.   If material flows between the outside and inside of a facility in an unplanned fashion at a point other than at a port  (e.g., a leak) this does not represent a connection port.</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.18362}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs20 A specific connection point where planned material flow occurs between the outside and inside of a facility.   Material normally  enters or leaves a facility only through a port.   If material flows between the outside and inside of a facility in an unplanned fashion at a point other than at a port  (e.g., a leak) this does not represent a connection port.\par
\par
A Connection Port is a kind of Facility.\par
\par
Connection Ports be used to inject or produce Material Streams.\par
}
</a:Description>
