<o:Entity Id="o1125">
<a:ObjectID>47F8475B-BB3A-49CD-9179-56E8B0D4BA4E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Asset</a:Name>
<a:Code>ASST</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The information resource or physical location that requires access management. Assets are managed through applications that may be deployed / implemented multiple times in parallel to deal with different assets for different businesses, processes or locations.

Assets can be at various levels: a cell, row, column, table, database or application, as well as site, area, building, corridor, room, locker, cupboard, equipment / hardware.

Physical assets are recorded in Information in the managing application and can therefore be treated as information assets. (e.g. ProWatch)</a:Comment>
