<o:Entity Id="o1810">
<a:ObjectID>821D653D-58F9-4C6C-8690-121135F8B716</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Asset Domain</a:Name>
<a:Code>ASST_DMN</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>An organizational set-up within a Business Domain which is responsible for the life-cycle management of an agreed delineated set of single or multiple facilities and/or reservoirs. For producing assets the management accountability of the organization resides with a delegated Asset Manager according to the Manual of Authorities.  Examples include: Groningen (UIO Netherlands)</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Calibri;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.22000}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\ul\f0\fs22 CSI:\ulnone  \par
Asset Domain is not commercially sensitive. It is a term used to define the organizational set-up responsible for the life-cycle management of specific facilities and/or reservoirs within a business domain.\par
\ul Confidentiality:\par
\ulnone The definition of an asset domain, as a general concept, is not typically considered confidential information. It is a term used to describe the organizational set-up responsible for the life-cycle management of specific facilities and/or reservoirs within a business domain.\par
\ul Criticality:\par
\ulnone Master data serves as the foundation for various business processes and systems within an organization. It is used for activities such as sales, marketing, supply chain management, financial reporting, and regulatory compliance. Accurate and reliable master data is crucial for effective decision-making, operational efficiency, and maintaining data integrity.\ul\par
Entity Category:\ulnone\par
Master data, as the data refers to the core data entities that are essential for the operations and decision-making processes of an organization.\par

\pard\f1\fs20\par
}
</a:Description>
