<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2450">
<a:ObjectID>72FA8FB5-AC43-43E9-8C1B-ADC04B0294C0</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Business_Identifier_Code</a:Name>
<a:Code>BSNSS_IDNTFR_CD</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Unique Identifier for a Bank is 8 character code that serves as a unique identification for banks and other financial institutions. BIC is suppplement with 3character branch identifier. It helps facilitate automated processing of information in various financial transactions. The BIC is specified by the International ISO standard ISO 9362. The BIC is defined externally. For Ex: DEUTDESM672 - Deutsche Bank, CITIGB2LXXX- CITIGROUP CENTRE, CANARY WHARF
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A8</a:DataType>
<a:Length>8</a:Length>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2451">
<a:ObjectID>FCF2A6D2-D788-4B03-8946-A9A2C55F8B1B</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Bank_Branch_Code</a:Name>
<a:Code>BNK_BRNCH_CD</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Part of unique identifier along with Business Identifier Code which uniquely identify the branch of a bank. This is defined by the bank.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A3</a:DataType>
<a:Length>3</a:Length>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2449">
<a:ObjectID>AC2FE5DE-2EE6-4393-9CAC-EE1996110984</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Bank_Account_Number</a:Name>
<a:Code>BNK_ACCNT_NMBR</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Part of unique identifier for Bank Account along with Business Identifier Code &amp; Bank branch Code which identifies the bank account number of a customer/supplier/vendor/Shell for the financial transaction. The bank account numbers are defined centrally in Shell. For Ex:5699999807 - SIEMENS GAS AND POWER GMBH
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A40</a:DataType>
<a:Length>40</a:Length>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o2452">
<a:ObjectID>B631C90D-D560-4B57-B6B1-87470BC2EF1B</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Currency_ISO_Code</a:Name>
<a:Code>CRRNCY_IS_CD</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775818177</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818177</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Unique identifier for Currency which is 3 character ISO 4217 code. Fox ex: CAD - Canadian Dollar, USD -  United States Dollar
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A3</a:DataType>
<a:Length>3</a:Length>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
<a:AutoMigrated>1</a:AutoMigrated>
