<o:Entity Id="o1255">
<a:ObjectID>AB747E9E-28E1-4A5C-9D24-01F21515C155</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Business Area</a:Name>
<a:Code>BSNSS_AR</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A Business Area represents a defined geographical region where Shell&#39;s business operations are conducted. It may encompass one or more facilities or geological fields, along with their associated production and utility facilities. Typically, a Business Area aligns with the business accountability of an Operations Manager or Production Unit Manager. In some cases, a Business Area may also cover the scope of a department that spans multiple geographical regions, particularly when the business activities are more office support in nature.</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Calibri;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.22000}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl252\slmult1\ul\f0\fs22 CSI:\ulnone  \par
Business Area is not commercially sensitive. It is a term used to define the organizational set-up responsible for the life-cycle management of specific facilities and/or reservoirs within a business domain.\par
\ul Confidentiality:\par
\ulnone The definition of a business area, as a general concept, is not typically considered confidential information. It is a term used to describe the organizational set-up responsible for the life-cycle management of specific facilities and/or reservoirs within an asset domain.\par
\ul Criticality:\par
\ulnone Master data serves as the foundation for various business processes and systems within an organization. It is used for activities such as sales, marketing, supply chain management, financial reporting, and regulatory compliance. Accurate and reliable master data is crucial for effective decision-making, operational efficiency, and maintaining data integrity.\ul\par
Entity Category:\ulnone\par
Master data, as the data refers to the core data entities that are essential for the operations and decision-making processes of an organization.\par

\pard\f1\fs20\par
}
</a:Description>
<a:Annotation>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Segoe UI;}}
\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs19 Example:\par
The Petrochemical Complex at Moerdijk,\par
The Refinery at Pernis,\par
The GTL site in Qatar,\par
The Nelson Production Area in the Central North Sea\par
\par
*** BUSINESS OWNER:\par
Real Estate\par
}</a:Annotation>
