<o:Entity Id="o657">
<a:ObjectID>3134528D-591C-4F6F-B432-9225743C95D8</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Company</a:Name>
<a:Code>CMPNY</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>An Organisation operating as a legal business. Examples: Aera Energy LLC, Schlumberger, McJunkin, TekSystems.

Includes Shell Companies and incorporated joint ventures in which Shell has a stake.

A Shell Company is a legal entity (Company) that is either wholly owned by Shell or an Incorporated Joint Venture in which Shell directly or indirectly holds a controlling interest. These are the Companies that Shell uses to legally conduct its business with other (Shell and non-Shell) companies. (Selling, Buying, Trading, Leasing,...)

Also: The smallest Shell organization for which a complete self-contained set of accounts can be drawn up for purposes of external reporting (e.g. Profit/Loss and Balance Sheet reports are generated for the Company Code).

The complete set of Shell Companies constitutes the Shell Group of Companies, aka &#39;Group&#39;.

aka: Subsidiary

A controlling interest allows Shell to require the implementation of the Shell Control Framework (SCF) by the venture, even if in practice Shell chooses not to apply some components of the SCF, for example by agreeing that the venture may operate to materially equivalent standards. Only these companies receive an Information Sharing type (derived) of &quot;S&quot;: GEI is 100% and IJV is &quot;N&quot;, or IJV is &quot;Y&quot; and Operatorship_Type is SOV.

Note that Shell Company is a smaller scope than published in the Finance Company File which also includes non-Shell Operated Ventures and UJVs (not legal entities)</a:Comment>
<a:Stereotype>EFDM+FDC</a:Stereotype>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.18362}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs20 An Organisation operating as a legal business. Examples: Aera Energy LLC, Schlumberger, McJunkin, TekSystems.\par
\par
Includes Shell Companies and incorporated joint ventures in which Shell has a stake.\par
\par
A Shell Company is a legal entity (Company) that is either wholly owned by Shell or an Incorporated Joint Venture in which Shell directly or indirectly holds a controlling interest. These are the Companies that Shell uses to legally conduct its business with other (Shell and non-Shell) companies. (Selling, Buying, Trading, Leasing,...)\par
\par
Also: The smallest Shell organization for which a complete self-contained set of accounts can be drawn up for purposes of external reporting (e.g. Profit/Loss and Balance Sheet reports are generated for the Company Code).\par
\par
The complete set of Shell Companies constitutes the Shell Group of Companies, aka &#39;Group&#39;.\par
\par
aka: Subsidiary\par
\par
A controlling interest allows Shell to require the implementation of the Shell Control Framework (SCF) by the venture, even if in practice Shell chooses not to apply some components of the SCF, for example by agreeing that the venture may operate to materially equivalent standards. Only these companies receive an Information Sharing type (derived) of &quot;S&quot;: GEI is 100% and IJV is &quot;N&quot;, or IJV is &quot;Y&quot; and Operatorship_Type is SOV.\par
\par
Note that Shell Company is a smaller scope than published in the Finance Company File which also includes non-Shell Operated Ventures and UJVs (not legal entities)\par
}
</a:Description>
<a:Annotation>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Segoe UI;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.22621}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs19\par
}
</a:Annotation>
