<o:Entity Id="o158">
<a:ObjectID>1F109BCA-390C-4C40-8D60-384E4A9BEC4B</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Completion</a:Name>
<a:Code>CMPLTN</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A system of wellbore openings and wellbore conduits which provide a means to produce or inject fluid from or into a reservoir, or a means to observe the conditions of the reservoir. A Wellbore which has never had Wellbore openings and is used to observe reservoir conditions is also considered a Completion.  A well may contain more than one Completion provided each is mechanically isolated to prevent hydraulic communication with another Completion.

A single Completion may provide the conduit for fluid flowing via one or more Actual Wellbore Opening Intervals, and the Actual Wellbore Opening Intervals servicing one Completion may be contained in more than one Wellbore. Further, a single Wellbore may contain multiple Actual Wellbore Opening Intervals that service more than one Completion.

Examples:
a.  A Wellbore is deepened and more wellbore openings are created at a deeper point, but there is no mechanical isolation of the fluids - it is still the same Completion with additional openings.
b.  The wellbore openings are plugged and the completion Temporarily Abandoned.  Later, even if in a different wellbore, new wellbore openings are created - it is the same Completion, with the same completion ID,  and it moves from the Temporarily Abandoned state to the Operational state.
If,  at any one point in time there are mechanically isolated fluid flows created/terminated in a well, then multiple Completions will be created/terminated.
c.  If there is one Completion in a well and a change is made to mechanically isolate the flow from part of the wellbore openings, then the original completion and completion ID remains with the wellbore openings that are not impacted by the mechanical isolation device.  A new Completion and completion ID are created for those wellbore openings that are isolated by the mechanical isolation device.
d.  If,  at a later point in time,  the mechanical isolation method is removed, then there is again only one Completion.  The newer Completion is terminated,  and the original Completion is changed to encompass the additional wellbore openings.</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.18362}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs20 A system of wellbore openings and wellbore conduits which provide a means to produce or inject fluid from or into a reservoir, or a means to observe the conditions of the reservoir. A Wellbore which has never had Wellbore openings and is used to observe reservoir conditions is also considered a Completion.  A well may contain more than one Completion provided each is mechanically isolated to prevent hydraulic communication with another Completion.\par
\par
A single Completion may provide the conduit for fluid flowing via one or more Actual Wellbore Opening Intervals, and the Actual Wellbore Opening Intervals servicing one Completion may be contained in more than one Wellbore. Further, a single Wellbore may contain multiple Actual Wellbore Opening Intervals that service more than one Completion.\par
\par
Examples:\par
a.  A Wellbore is deepened and more wellbore openings are created at a deeper point, but there is no mechanical isolation of the fluids - it is still the same Completion with additional openings.\par
b.  The wellbore openings are plugged and the completion Temporarily Abandoned.  Later, even if in a different wellbore, new wellbore openings are created - it is the same Completion, with the same completion ID,  and it moves from the Temporarily Abandoned state to the Operational state.\par
If,  at any one point in time there are mechanically isolated fluid flows created/terminated in a well, then multiple Completions will be created/terminated.\par
c.  If there is one Completion in a well and a change is made to mechanically isolate the flow from part of the wellbore openings, then the original completion and completion ID remains with the wellbore openings that are not impacted by the mechanical isolation device.  A new Completion and completion ID are created for those wellbore openings that are isolated by the mechanical isolation device.\par
d.  If,  at a later point in time,  the mechanical isolation method is removed, then there is again only one Completion.  The newer Completion is terminated,  and the original Completion is changed to encompass the additional wellbore openings.\par
}
</a:Description>
