<o:Entity Id="o1939">
<a:ObjectID>ABCF7F99-D041-4C7C-ADCC-9FD1B561D4E0</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Completion Primary Fluid Conveyance Method</a:Name>
<a:Code>CMPLTN_PRMRY_FLD_CNVYNC_MTHD</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1775817984</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1775818154</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The normal means by which fluids are conveyed to and from a particular WELL COMPLETION.  For example, &quot;Beam pump&quot;, &quot;Plunger lift&quot;, etc.
The COMPLETION PRIMARY FLUID CONVEYANCE METHOD does not change just because the COMPLETION is used intermittently to produce or inject via another method.  (A business may periodically inject steam into an oil producer, but this does not change the primary conveyance method.)</a:Comment>
<a:Description>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}
{\*\generator Riched20 10.0.18362}\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs20 The normal means by which fluids are conveyed to and from a particular WELL COMPLETION.  For example, &quot;Beam pump&quot;, &quot;Plunger lift&quot;, etc.\par
The COMPLETION PRIMARY FLUID CONVEYANCE METHOD does not change just because the COMPLETION is used intermittently to produce or inject via another method.  (A business may periodically inject steam into an oil producer, but this does not change the primary conveyance method.)\par
}
</a:Description>
<a:Annotation>{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\nouicompat\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Segoe UI;}}
\viewkind4\uc1 
\pard\f0\fs19 *** PURPOSE:\par
Beam Pump\par
Plunger Lift\par
Progressive Cavity Pump\par
Jet Pump\par
Chamber  Lift\par
Electric submersible pump\par
Flowing\par
Gas Lift\par
Hydraulic Pump Lift\par
Injection system\par
Jack Line\par
Lineshaft Turbine Pump\par
}</a:Annotation>
